# SQL's `using`: DS0122 with a fix to `on`.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv' | join 'customers.csv' using customerId
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..53
  PIPELINE@0..52
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    JOIN_OP@15..52
      IDENT@15..19 "join"
      WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
      LITERAL@20..35
        STRING@20..35 "'customers.csv'"
      WHITESPACE@35..36 " "
      IDENT@36..41 "using"
      WHITESPACE@41..42 " "
      NAME_REF@42..52
        IDENT@42..52 "customerId"
  WHITESPACE@52..53 "\n"

error[DS0122]: `join` uses `on`, not `using`
  --> query:1:37
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | join 'customers.csv' using customerId
  |                                     ^^^^^
  |
  = help: write `on` before the columns to match

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    'orders.csv' | join 'customers.csv' on customerId
which parses without errors
